  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{PtCl}_{4}\\right]^{2-}$ has square planar geometry. $\\mathrm{Pt}: 5 d^{9} 6 s^{1}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/-gdRq6NOhCl92znyLCzO5N9qVC0JmexUVrElhAzON38.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nTwo electrons are removed from $5 d$ shell and $6 s$ shell. So, hybridisation takes place is $d s p^{2}$ i.e. square planar geometry.",
    "image": null
  },
